limbs:
I know how lost forever, and at length
How still these lovely tossing limbs shall lie,
And the bright laughter and the panting breath;

lime:
Choice little dainty bits
Beneath the spreading roots of a broad lime;
Nibbling his fill he stops from time to time

limber:
I like to jest go joggin' 'long,
To limber up my soul with song;
To stop awhile 'n' chat the men,

limpid:
I will tell you when they met:
In the limpid days of Spring;
Elder boughs were budding yet,
